course: dictionary
lesson: 6187
title: Misbehave and the little word mis-
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To misbehave means to behave badly, to be naughty or not follow the rules. «The pupils who misbehaved in class lost their playtime.» The clues are lost playtime and breaking rules, so misbehaved must mean acting badly.
explain: Break the word into parts to crack it. Mis- means wrongly, as in misread and misspell. Behave means to act in a good or proper way. Put them together and misbehave means to behave wrongly.
explain: Some words change their meaning in different places. «The printer is misbehaving again» does not mean the printer is naughty. It means the machine is not working as it should. Always check the sentence around the word to see which meaning fits.
fact: Misbehave is a verb, so it changes: misbehaves, misbehaved, misbehaving.
fact: The prefix mis- means wrongly, as in misread, misspell and misbehave.
fact: To misbehave means to behave badly, to be naughty or not follow the rules.
fact: Testing boundaries means misbehaving on purpose to see what is allowed.
fact: Informal use: a machine that misbehaves does not work as it should.
exercise: «The pupils who misbehave in class may lose their playtime.» What does misbehave mean? | *To behave badly or break the rules | To read a book quietly | To go home early | To sing loudly in assembly
exercise: Which part of misbehave tells you it means wrongly? | behave | *mis- | bad | -ave
exercise: «The printer is misbehaving again.» What does misbehaving suggest here? | It is playing a game | It is singing loudly | It is being naughty in class | *It is not working as it should
test: Which word means to behave badly? | *misbehave | behave | obey | behaving well
test: Mis- means wrongly. What does misspell mean? | *To spell wrongly | To write a long story | To say a word out loud | To spell very neatly
exam: Ella says a printer that misbehaves is naughty. Is she right? | Yes, it is being rude to the teacher | No, misbehave means to sleep | Yes, it has been sent to the head | *No, it means the printer is not working as it should
